      "id": 1,
      "text": "In 1859 lumberman Charles Mears and Giles Slocum platted a settlement at the head of White Lake, naming it Mears.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://michigan4you.com/history-of-whitehall-michigan/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1862 the settlement was renamed Whitehall and later incorporated as a village in 1867.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whitehall%2C_Michigan"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Whitehall sits five miles from Lake Michigan, at the mouth of the White River where it opens into the lake.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.whitelake.org/business/city-of-whitehall/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The White River Light Station, first lit in 1875, guarded the narrow channel that connects White Lake to Lake Michigan.",
